                <pb facs="0884" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg796"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eddy to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports that the Russian Government formally agrees to the submission
                    of the circumstances of the North Sea incident to a special tribunal as provided
                    by articles 9 and 14 of The Hague convention; that the preliminary inquiry is to
                    be conducted at Vigo, where the fleet is to remain at present.)</p>
            </div>
